# Dev Workflow & Commands

## Always

1. `npm install` on fresh clone before building  
2. Match existing patterns before adding files  
3. Screens → `app/`; UI → `components/`; logic → `hooks/` or `services/`; types → `types/`  
4. `npm run lint` after changes (0 errors required; known warnings in donate/give & events OK until touched)  
5. Manual test via `npm start` / Expo Go — do not add test frameworks unless asked  

## Commands

```bash
npm install
npm run lint
npm run clean          # prefer over ./gradlew clean (missing dirs OK)
npm start              # or npx expo start; clear cache: npx expo start -c
npm run android
npm run build:debug | build:release | build:bundle
npm run clean:build:debug   # clean + build variants
```

Gradle from `android/`: `./gradlew assembleDebug`, `bundleRelease` (first run downloads Gradle ~30–60s).

EAS: `eas build --platform android --profile production` (~10–20 min). Profiles in `eas.json`: development, preview, production, production-apk.

## Pre-commit

Lint clean; strict types; no stray `console.log`; explicit returns; hook deps; async error handling; no secrets; unused imports/vars removed.

## Android native

Only change `android/` when needed (permissions, gradle, resources). Test with `npm run build:debug`. Document in commit message.
